## O4 gate-fix session: merge with latest manus-parity, all gates green

`.jgatefail.txt` reported: `MERGE CONFLICT with latest manus-parity: run git merge
manus-parity, resolve all conflicts keeping both sides, commit.`

### Root cause
No source file conflicted in any merge round. `git merge manus-parity` brought in other
workstreams' code (N2 canvas, N4 recipe engine, C19 failover, J5 command-risk, N10
output-type/effort routing, N9 ask-user, C20 and more) and every one of those files
auto-merged cleanly with `ort`. The only file that ever conflicted was the tracked rollup
`.jdone`, because every branch prepends its own report at the same top-of-file anchor:

- **add/add** when both sides modified `.jdone` (parity tip `ed26550`, and again at
  `61aca0c`, `585fd55`). Resolved as a **superset**: this report stays at the top and the
  whole parity rollup follows verbatim, with only the conflict-marker lines removed.
- **modify/delete** when a parity commit deleted `.jdone` outright while this branch
  modified it (parity tip `26befe6`). Resolved by keeping the modified version, since
  `.jdone` is this task's required deliverable.

`manus-parity` advanced several times while this session ran, so the merge was re-run and
re-resolved each time it did.

### Round 5 (parity tip `411df5e`, C21 mirofish)
`manus-parity` re-added its own rollup to `.jdone` (the M3/C21 report block), so this round
was a **content** conflict on that file only. Resolved as a union: this O4 report stays at the
top and parity's M3/C21 report block follows verbatim, with only the three conflict-marker
lines removed. Every source file again auto-merged with `ort`, including the O4 socket and
protocol surfaces (`src/protocol/types.ts`, `packages/shared/src/socket.ts`).

Deep validation also caught a real gap in an earlier round: 25 lines of this branch's own
earlier header wording had been rewritten rather than preserved. They are now archived
verbatim in a labeled `Superseded header wording (preserved verbatim)` section, so `.jdone`
is a **strict** superset of both merge parents rather than merely of their bodies.

Nothing in the O4 change set was at risk. The O4 files
(`src/protocol/__tests__/seqReplay.test.ts`, `src/protocol/store.ts`,
`packages/web/src/services/chatSocket.ts`, `packages/web/src/services/chatSocket.test.ts`,
`packages/web/src/app/app/[sessionUid]/TaskPageClient.tsx`) are byte-identical to commit
`5114c89`. `src/protocol/types.ts`, `src/protocol/socket.ts` and
`packages/shared/src/socket.ts` differ from `5114c89` only by purely additive
other-workstream lines (for example the N4 `RecipeUpdateEvent` / `RecipeRestartEvent` and
the N9 `ResolveAskUser` / `AskUserRequestedEvent`), which is why they auto-merged; the O4
`lastSeq` / `seq` / `eventsAfterSeq` additions are all still present in the merged tree.

### What was done
Every `.jdone` conflict was resolved by **keeping both sides**, never by choosing one side
and dropping the other, and never by weakening a test. Verification was mechanical after
each resolution: the merged `.jdone` is a multiset-superset of the ours blob, the theirs
blob and the previous HEAD blob (0 non-empty lines missing from any of them), with 0
conflict markers and 0 U+FFFD replacement characters left in the tree.

No source file was edited by this session and no test was weakened, deleted or skipped.

