The gate (`MERGE CONFLICT with latest manus-parity: run git merge manus-parity,
resolve all conflicts keeping both sides, commit`) requires `manus-parity` to be a
live ancestor of this branch. The branch advanced three times while this was being
worked, so the merge was performed three times; each one is committed and the
ancestor condition holds against the final tip `585fd55`.

## The three merges

1. `330e135` - parity tip `26befe6`. Conflicts: `src/protocol/events.ts`,
   `src/protocol/types.ts` (union of both sides) and `.jdone` (modify/delete; kept
   the branch version, the convention on every sibling branch).
