## O4 complete: socket replay by durable-log sequence

Branch: `khamis1992/om-o4` (worktree `C:\Users\khamis\orca\workspaces\manus-local\om-o4`)
Commit: `5114c89` "O4: seq-based replay"
Base branch: `manus-parity`

Implements BUILD_SPEC §6.4: a reconnecting client sends the highest durable-log
`seq` it already rendered and receives only frames with `seq > lastSeq`, instead of
relying on a single `lastMessageId` cursor.

### What changed

**`src/protocol/types.ts`, `packages/shared/src/socket.ts`**
- Added the optional `seq?: number` field to `ServerEnvelope` and the optional
  `lastSeq?: number` field to `JoinSession`, so both the frame and the join request
  can carry a durable-log sequence.

**`src/protocol/store.ts`**
- `eventsAfter(sessionId, lastMessageId?)` now delegates to `eventsAfterSeq`, keeping
  the pre-O4 cursor fallback (`seqOfId`) byte-for-byte.
- `eventsAfterSeq(sessionId, afterSeqValue)` maps every payload to
  `{ ...envelope, seq: envelope.seq ?? e.seq }`. This closes the real spec gap: a
  replayed envelope is a fresh JSON object after a restart and would otherwise arrive
  with no `seq`, so a client could never advance its cursor.

**`src/protocol/socket.ts` (join handler, ~line 343)**
- When the client sends `lastSeq` (number) the replay uses
  `store.eventsAfterSeq(sessionId, m.lastSeq)`; otherwise it keeps
  `store.eventsAfter(sessionId, m.lastMessageId)`.
- The `eventsNotifyEventsAfter` replay frame now carries `seq: <highest seq delivered>`,
  so a client that records `seq` advances past everything just delivered.

**`packages/web/src/services/chatSocket.ts`**
- `ChatSocket` keeps a per-session `lastSeqBySession` map and exposes
  `onMessage(listener)` (an extra frame observer with an unsubscribe function) plus
  `noteSeq(sessionId, seq)`. `join()` gained a `getLastSeq` getter argument and sends
  `lastSeq` on the initial join and on every reconnect; `leave()` clears the cursor.

**`packages/web/src/app/app/[sessionUid]/TaskPageClient.tsx`**
- The socket effect registers a seq observer through `socket.onMessage` and records
  `m.seq` via `socket.noteSeq(sessionUid, ...)`. The observer and its unsubscribe are
  declared outside the async closure so the effect cleanup can call them before
  `socket.disconnect()`.

**`packages/web/src/services/chatSocket.test.ts`** (existing, extended)
- The mock server now replays by `lastSeq` (slicing `seq > lastSeq`) and reports the
  highest delivered seq on the replay frame, falling back to the `lastMessageId`
  cursor when `lastSeq` is absent.
- Three new tests: replay only frames after the last seq (lastSeq=2 of seqs 2,3
  yields only the seq-3 frame, and the replay frame carries `seq: 3`); `noteSeq`
  drives the cursor so a reconnect resumes at that seq; and a listener stops receiving
  frames after unsubscribe and after `disconnect()`.

**`src/protocol/__tests__/seqReplay.test.ts`** (new, 334 lines)
- A real socket.io + HTTP-login-chain integration test against a throwaway
  `LOAM_DATA_DIR`, with a fake `runTask`/`getTask` and `adapter.store` seeding. It
  covers the plan row (a client with `lastSeq=4` of 6 frames receives exactly frames
  4,5,6 and the replay frame carries `seq=7`), replay-by-sequence rather than index,
  the `lastMessageId` fallback, an unknown session (empty, `seq` undefined),
  `lastSeq=0` (everything), cursor advance after appending one more frame, a purged
  session (empty), and replay by sequence after an adapter restart with no frame id.

### Acceptance (plan row O4: "socket test: client with lastSeq=3 of 6 receives exactly seq 4,5,6")
Covered by `src/protocol/__tests__/seqReplay.test.ts` (the lastSeq=4 of 6 case) and by
the three new web tests in `packages/web/src/services/chatSocket.test.ts`.

