# N2 - Canvas view: DONE

Workspace "Canvas" tab rendering the N1 run graph: pan/zoom, auto-layout, an E
shortcut that opens a node, live SSE updates, a Recipe side panel, and Arabic/RTL.

## The failure that was fixed
The canvas work committed as `33a8911` left one pre-existing web test red:

```
packages/web/src/components/workspace/__tests__/autoOpen.test.ts
  > workspace auto-open decision > latestWorkspaceDecision returns the newest qualifying event
  AssertionError: expected { id: 'id-0.21480746367457115', …(6) } to be { id: 'id-0.6785752071943618', …(6) }
```

`isCanvasSignalTool` had been written with a broad `name.startsWith('browser_')`
(plus `gen_*`, `loam_*`, `office_*`, `docx|xlsx|pptx`, `file_write`, `file_edit`,
`code_session`, `web_scaffold`). The test pins `browser_navigate` as a
**non-qualifying** tool (it is a display label in `packages/web/src/components/chat/toolLabels.ts`,
not a tool the agent registers), so the newest qualifying event became the
`browser_navigate` event instead of the `office_export` one. That is a real
product bug, not a stale test: the canvas was hijacking tool events that should
resolve to a workspace artifact.

## What the fix produces
`isCanvasSignalTool` now matches only the tools the agent really registers, so
the canvas stays the surface for long-horizon work with no single file to point
at:

- `BROWSER_TOOL_STEMS` is an explicit list taken from `src/tools/browser.ts`
  (`browser_open`, `browser_goto`, `browser_snapshot`, `browser_click`,
  `browser_type`, `browser_press`, `browser_eval`, `browser_screenshot`,
  `browser_table`, `browser_act`, `browser_pages`, `browser_close`, `browser_som`,
  `browser_trace`) plus `browser_operator` from `browserOperator.ts`. Matching is
  `name === stem || name.startsWith(stem + '_')`, so `browser_navigate` and the
  rest of the label-only names cannot match. `browser_operator` keeps its
  timestamped tool-use name (`browser_operator_<timestamp>`) working.
- `web_*` (`src/tools/web.ts`: `web_search`, `web_fetch`), `deep_research`
  (`deepResearch.ts`), `wide_research` (`wideResearch.ts`) and `code_session*`
  (`codeSession.ts`).
- Everything else is dropped, because a file path or an `office_*`/`video` tool
  already resolves above it: `decideWorkspaceOpen` returns the editor first, so
  the canvas never steals an artifact. This is what restores the test.

Coverage added to the pre-existing suite (no assertion relaxed, none removed):
`__tests__/autoOpen.test.ts` gained a `Neo N2 canvas auto-open decision` block
(5 tests) pinning the real names as qualifying, the label/file-producing names as
non-qualifying, the canvas target for a long-horizon tool, the
artifact-wins-over-canvas precedence, and `latestWorkspaceDecision` returning the
canvas for the newest long-horizon tool. 18/18 pass.

## Second defect found and fixed during the same pass
`CanvasPanel` resolved its locale and translated with it, but never synced the
document direction. The panel lays itself out with logical CSS (`border-s`,
`ms-`/`me-`, `ps-`/`pe-`), which resolves against `document.documentElement.dir`,
so under Arabic the canvas chrome was laid out left-to-right while its text was
Arabic. The panel now calls `setLocale(locale)` from `@/i18n/t` whenever it owns
the locale, so `dir`/`lang` follow the locale the panel renders in. The
`getLocale` prop is a test seam and is deliberately skipped, so a test provider
never rewrites the real document. The canvas **surface** stays `dir="ltr"`:
its geometry is graph space, not text flow. A new test
(`points the document direction at the rendered locale`) pins both.

## Acceptance criteria (N2)
The task asks for Playwright; the harness has no browser, so the same behaviour
is pinned with vitest + @testing-library against the real panel with an injected
client/stream (documented here as the task allows):

- **6+ nodes live for a run with 6 steps** - `CanvasPanel.test.tsx` renders the
  real panel over a seven-node graph (root question + six recipe steps), asserts
  7 `canvas-node` cards, the Recipe list `1. Step 1` .. `6. Step 6`, the stats
  line `7 nodes`, and that a live stream drives the `Live` indicator.
- **Organize lays out without overlap** - clicking `Organize` re-runs the layered
  layout and every node card's transform is distinct (no two cards share a cell).
- **E opens the detail** - `keydown e` opens the newest node's sheet
  (`canvas-node-detail`, `data-node-id="step-six"`); `Escape` closes it. Clicking
  a card opens the same sheet.
- **RTL labels render** - with `getLocale: () => 'ar'` the Recipe header reads
  `الوصفة`, the stats line `7 عقد`, node titles use Arabic labels, and the node
  sheet marks the node `من اليمين إلى اليسار`. A separate test pins that the
  document direction follows the rendered locale while the surface stays `ltr`.

## Files
