N4 — Incremental Recipe engine: DONE

Summary
-------
Added orchestrator mode `recipe`: after each step the planner proposes the next
step(s) from that step's results (add / rewrite / drop), the recipe grows within
the session budget, `remaining_estimate` is reported and decreases, and
`restartFrom(nodeId)` regenerates only the downstream while upstream outputs are
kept verbatim.

  - `src/agent/recipe.ts` (521 lines, new): the recipe state machine, free of
    model and tool dependencies. `initRecipe`, `beginStep`, `finishStep`,
    `applyProposal`, `parseProposal`, `proposePrompt`, `observationsFromTrace`,
    `remainingEstimate`, `pendingCount`, `completedCount`, `restartFrom`,
    `restoreTail`, `reseedRecipe`, `planStepsOf`, `stepContract`, `statusRank`.
  - `src/agent/orchestrator.ts`: recipe mode wired end to end. The upfront plan
    is the SEED; every round emits `recipe_update` and the frozen `plan` is kept
    as the recipe's projection so the client never sees two different tasks. A
    failed step is EVIDENCE, not a reason to rebuild the plan: it is marked
    `blocked`, the planner is asked what to do, and the run re-routes around it.
    A dropped step is skipped rather than executed. A replan re-seeds the recipe
    instead of discarding it. `recipeRestart` is applied once, at the first
    opportunity, and never re-runs the steps before the restart point.
  - `src/agent/planner.ts`: `proposeNextSteps` (the planner round for one
    recipe step) alongside the existing `planTask`.
  - `src/agent/events.ts`, `src/protocol/events.ts`, `src/protocol/types.ts`,
    `src/protocol/socket.ts`, `packages/shared/src/socket.ts`,
    `packages/shared/src/eventCategories.ts`: `RecipeStepInfo`, `RecipeChange`,
    `RecipeState`, the `recipe_update` and `recipe_restart` events, their
    client types and their category (`planner`).
  - `src/graph/runGraph.ts`: the run graph accepts a recipe step node id.

Acceptance criteria (automated, all passing)
--------------------------------------------
  - a tool fails -> re-route to an alternate tool:
    `src/agent/__tests__/orchestratorRecipe.test.ts` (recipe re-route after a
    failed step: the step is `blocked`, the planner is asked, and the run
    continues instead of rebuilding the plan).
  - restart from step 3 does not re-call tools of steps 1-2 (mock call counter):
    the same suite asserts the mock tool call counter and the kept/regenerated
    step ids for a restart at `s3` (`recipe restarted at s3; kept 2,
    regenerated 1`), and `restartFrom` keeps the upstream steps' ids, status and
    node while reopening only the restart point
    (`src/agent/__tests__/recipeEngine.test.ts`, `recipeIds.test.ts`).
  - estimate shown and decreases: `recipe_update.remainingEstimate` is emitted
    on init, on every round and on every advance; `remainingEstimate` keeps the
    smaller of the planner's number and the steps actually open, so it can move
    up when a round reveals real new work and never reports more work than the
    recipe holds (`recipeEngine.test.ts`).
  - ids stay unique: `withUniqueIds` enforces it, because a recipe step id keys
    the canvas node, the frozen plan and the restart target
    (`recipeIds.test.ts`).
  - a restart that cannot regenerate its tail does not silently shrink the run:
    `restoreTail` puts the discarded downstream steps back as pending work, and
    the orchestrator emits `recipe_restart` before doing so
    (`recipeIds.test.ts`, `orchestratorRecipe.test.ts`).

