    `recipeRestart` once per run and keeps the upstream steps' ids/status/node,
    so a replay layer can re-execute only the regenerated tail from the
    checkpoint. `recipeState` is persisted with every checkpoint through
    `saveRecipe`, so a resume continues the same recipe instead of reseeding.
  - `proposeNextSteps` is the seam for any other planner implementation; it takes
    `RecipeProposeContext` and returns `PlanResult`-shaped usage, so a
    structured-output planner can replace the JSON `parseProposal` path without
    touching the engine.
