# C19 gate-fix session: hermetic budget suite + merge with manus-parity

`.jgatefail.txt` reported: MERGE CONFLICT with latest manus-parity. The only file
that conflicted was the tracked rollup `.jdone` (add/add: this branch's C19 report
vs parity's O3/O6/O2/D5/O1/V11/fc-05 rollup). No source file conflicted.

## The third full-sweep failure, root-caused and fixed

`src/agent/__tests__/orchestratorBudget.test.ts` failed 1/6 with
"the step is critiqued twice (attempt + revision)". It was **not** caused by C19:
the file is byte-identical to manus-parity and only `src/config.ts` differs.
The real root cause is that the suite was **not hermetic**:

- The revision worker prompt names the fix and the files involved, which trips the
  coding-turn heuristic in `src/llm/codingRouter.ts`, so the revision worker was
  routed through the **coding router -> the real failover chain** (6 providers by
  default: ollama, opencode-go, freellmapi, longcat, openrouter, ornith). With any
  provider reachable, the failover walk answered the revision, so the expected
  critique/revision accounting broke and the run escaped to live providers.
- The suite also wrote into the repo's real `data/` and `workspace/`.

Fix (mirrors the existing hermetic pattern in `orchestratorHooks.test.ts`):
1. `import "../../test/isolation.js";` first, before `config.js` is evaluated, so
   `DATA_DIR`/`workspace/` are redirected to a per-process temp dir.
2. Inject the routing seams the orchestrator already exposes:
   `createProviderClient`, `cooldownStore` (in-memory), `env`, `onCodingRoute`.
3. Give the fixture `cfg.coding = { enabled: true, chain: [], logEdits: false }` and
   `cfg.failover = { providers: [] }`, so a coding turn has no coder to pick and
   is answered by the injected fake client instead of the network.

Verified in a repo-copy sandbox (the same check `check:test-isolation` runs):
- pre-fix: the suite left `data/` and `workspace/` residue and failed 1/6;
- post-fix: **no residue**, 6/6 pass.

## Gate condition verified

`git merge-base --is-ancestor manus-parity HEAD` exits 0 and
`git merge manus-parity` reports "Already up to date." No conflict marker remains
in the tree and `git status --porcelain` is empty.

## Gates (all run from the worktree root on the committed tree)

- `npx tsc --noEmit`                       -> exit 0
- `node --import tsx --test src/agent/__tests__/orchestratorBudget.test.ts`
                                             -> tests 6, pass 6, fail 0
- touched-area suites (orchestratorBudget + orchestratorHooks + configFailover)
                                             -> tests 14, pass 14, fail 0
- `npm run check:orchestrator`             -> exit 0
- `npm run check:encoding`                 -> exit 0
- `node --import tsx --test "src/**/*.test.ts"` -> tests 2166, pass 2164, fail 2
  (both remaining failures are pre-existing and documented; see below)

## Remaining full-sweep failures (both pre-existing, neither caused by C19)

1. `src/agent/__tests__/toolDescriptions.test.ts` -> "suggest_plan is neither
   registered nor listed in PENDING_CODING_TOOLS". The file,
   `src/agent/taskToolScope.ts` and `src/tools/planTools.ts` are byte-identical
   to manus-parity; this is the inherited D4 defect already documented in the
   preserved rollup. Untouched here.
2. `src/server/__tests__/worktrees.test.ts` -> "reports non-git folders without
   throwing". Environmental: `%TEMP%` on this machine sits inside the git repo
   `C:/Users/khamis`, so `git -C <tmp> rev-parse` succeeds and `isGit` is true.
   Reproduced identically on the untouched base commit; this task touches no file
   under `src/server`.

Note (second merge): parity advanced again (tip `045f3e2`, +20 commits: the
`src/policy/commandRisk/` shell-risk gate, `shell.ts`, `shellRisk` and `riskTier`
work). `git merge manus-parity` conflicted in `.jdone` only; resolved the same way
(both sides verbatim, 0 lines lost). Parity's own isolation gate fails identically
(same `data`/`workspace` residue assertion, 3 failures), so that residue is
pre-existing on parity and not attributable to C19.


`npm run check:test-isolation` still reports the pre-existing `data`/`workspace`
residue (it failed identically at the pre-fix HEAD, 4 failures vs 2 now); the
