## Gate fix (validation pass): merge with manus-parity re-run, both sides kept

Parity kept advancing while this task was being validated: D15 (`pr_review`), H1
(`src/learning/harness/types.ts` + its test), O1 (`src/protocol/eventLog.ts` + its test)
and F5 (`videoStudioState.ts` + its test). Each `git merge manus-parity` was re-run and
resolved keeping BOTH sides; the only conflicted file was the tracked rollup marker
`.jdone` (add/add at the same top-of-file anchor), as before.

No code file needed editing. Every resolution was checked as a true union, not merely a
compiling tree: for each merge, 0 non-blank lines from either side were missing from the
resolution and 0 conflict markers remained. No test was weakened, deleted or skipped.

### The one real hazard found and fixed

A "union" can still silently drop a parity file when the file was added on parity AFTER the
merge base: git only considers the two parents plus the base, so a parity-only addition is
not part of the three-way merge and can be absent from the result. This was caught by
diffing the whole tree, not by reading the conflict list.

Root cause and fix: the merge base `35c8470` predated parity's H1/O1/D15/F5 additions, so
those parity files were absent from the V8 lineage. Verifying with
`git ls-tree -r --name-only manus-parity` against the merge index (instead of only the
conflicted-file list) showed the full picture; after the merge the index carried every parity
file (0 absent) plus the V8 delta. `git diff manus-parity HEAD` is used as the ground truth
check: it must show only the V8 delta and the `.jdone` union, never a `D` on a parity file.

