Resolution judgment call (documented so it can be reviewed): the `src/agent/loop.ts`
per-step usage block conflicted because HEAD accumulated `usage.promptTokens`/
`usage.completionTokens`/`usage.durationMs` inline while parity called
`addUsage(usage, result.usage)`. Keeping both literally would DOUBLE-COUNT tokens, so the
resolution keeps parity's `addUsage` (which accumulates prompt/completion/duration plus the
cache counters) and retains HEAD's `consumeTokens` budget charge. This is "both features",
not a double tally; `addUsage`'s implementation was read and verified to cover every field
HEAD set inline. All unioned import symbols were confirmed used (occurrence count >= 1 each).

## D19 feature recap
- Sleep/wake: `src/server/sessionSleep.ts` idle N minutes (default 30, configurable via
  `agent.idleSleepMinutes`) -> `sleeping`, persisting state BEFORE releasing browser/pty
  resources; a user message wakes and restores exactly the persisted snapshot. State changes
  are emitted with the transition reason; timers are cancelled by agent activity; sleeping is
  idempotent.
- Compute budget: `src/agent/computeBudget.ts` per-session step/token budget, warn at 80%,
  hard stop at 100%, `raise` resumes. Enforced on the linear `runAgent` loop and the
  orchestrator (planner/worker/verifier/replan all charged). Surface: `/api/sessions/:id/runtime`
  routes (`src/server/routes/sessionRuntime.ts`) + `SessionStatusBadge` in the web task page.

