## fc-05: Video Studio state sync (preserve manual edits)
fc-05 complete. Builds on the fc-02 relay (`src/server/videoStudioRelay.ts`) and the
fc-03 `video_studio` tool (`src/tools/videoStudio.ts`). The agent now reads the live
editor timeline before every command, reports a manual-edit notice when the user
edited the panel by hand, and persists the project (debounced) into the task's files.
### What fc-05 delivers
- `src/tools/videoStudioState.ts` (new, 603 lines):
  - `summarizeProjectState(raw)`: turns the editor's loose `inspect` payload into a
    compact, accurate summary (`durationSec`, `playheadSec`, `selection`, `tracks`,
    `clips` with track/start/end and source in-out, `textLayers`, `audioClips`,
    `transitions`, `effects`). Every extractor is defensive: an unrecognisable payload
    degrades to an empty (or partial) summary instead of throwing. Clips inherit the
    track's `kind` when they do not repeat it, so the text/audio buckets are accurate.
  - `hashProjectState(summary)`: a stable 16-char sha256 fingerprint of the canonical
    summary (sorted keys, no `undefined`), so a change is detected without storing the
    whole project and unrelated editor internals never look like a manual edit.
  - `diffProjectStates(prev, next)` / `formatStateDiff(diff)`: report added / removed /
    moved clips (with from->to position), text, audio, transitions, effects and
    playhead/duration changes as compact `+` / `-` / `~` tokens.
  - `VideoStudioStateTracker`: keeps the last state the agent saw per task and produces
    the manual-edit notice. An empty read is never reported as a manual edit and is
    never adopted as the baseline, so a transient/unsupported editor response cannot
    produce a false notice or mask the next real change.
  - `VideoStudioProjectStore`: persists the project into
    `loam-video/project.json` in the task workspace, debounced (default 500ms,
    resets the timer on each change). Each write stores the raw `inspect` payload plus
    the derived summary and an ISO `savedAt`, written via a temp file + rename. Writes
    are best-effort: a filesystem failure is swallowed and never breaks an agent
    command. `load` returns the typed `VideoStudioPersistedProject`, or null when the
    file is missing/unreadable.
  - Shared `videoStudioProjectStore` instance for the running server.
- `src/tools/videoStudio.ts` (extended):
  - `readStudioState(taskId, relay, tracker, store, workspace)` reads the live timeline
    via the fc-02 relay `inspect` (best-effort: a relay failure returns undefined and
    the action proceeds without a summary), updates the per-task tracker and schedules
    a debounced persist.
  - `run()` reads the state before and after every action. A `state` action reuses the
    pre-read so it is a single `inspect` round trip instead of two. Every result body
    now carries `summary` and `notice`; when the tracker reports a change, the notice
    is prepended to the result content.
  - The tool description now tells the model every result carries the compact timeline
    summary, that a notice is prepended when the timeline changed since its last
    action, and never to rebuild the project from memory.
  - `stateTracker` / `projectStore` are injectable for tests.
### Acceptance tests (fc-05 spec)
- Unit: diff summary for added/removed/moved clips; the tool result carries the
  summary; the manual-change notice appears only when the hash differs.
- Covered by `src/tools/__tests__/videoStudioState.test.ts` (19 tests) and
  `src/tools/__tests__/videoStudio.test.ts` (39 tests, including the dispatch order
  `["inspect", "commands", "inspect"]` for `open`), plus
  `src/server/__tests__/videoStudioE2E.test.ts` (4 tests, including a manual edit made
  between two commands asserting the notice
  `User edited the timeline manually since your last action` and the diff
  `~clip clip_1 0s->3s`).
