## The one remaining node failure is pre-existing and NOT caused by this merge
`src/server/__tests__/worktrees.test.ts` -> "reports non-git folders without throwing"
(`true == false` at `src/server/__tests__/worktrees.test.ts:44`). Both that test file
and `src/server/worktrees.ts` are byte-identical on both merge sides (same blob hash
`2f3e37d24e` in HEAD and in `ed26550`, `git status` clean, no diff between the two),
so the merge cannot have caused it. The cause is environmental: `%TEMP%` is
`C:\Users\khamis\AppData\Local\Temp` and `git -C %TEMP% rev-parse --show-toplevel`
walks upward and resolves to `C:/Users/khamis`, which is itself a git repository, so a
fresh temp folder is reported as a git folder. Confirmed by a direct probe in this
session, and the same failure is recorded in the V8, N2 and C19 reports below. The
test was not weakened, deleted or skipped, and no file under `src/server` was edited.

No secrets committed. No forbidden path touched. No `.neo-*` or `.jcode-*` marker
file staged, and nothing under `tmp/` is tracked. No real external model API was called
by the tests (the rerank path uses a local embedder stub).

